I suggest that it would be funny to include an Amulet of Silly Death in 
the game. This would:

1) Increase the generation of floating eyes, nymphs, and cockatrices.
2) Cause vault guards to become impatient one turn sooner.
3) When bumping into a peaceful creature or pet, this would have
    a chance (10%/20%/30% if B/U/C) of skipping attack confirmation,
    a la Stormbringer.
4) Damage from kicking the wall, empty air, or an immovable object
    is doubled.
5) Asmodeus is generated hostile, and wielding the Vorpal Blade if
    it is available (it will be chaotic in this instance).
6) The effect of carrying a lizard corpse in inventory becomes half as
    effective, and completely ineffective during a full moon.
7) If the hero's life is saved (pretty unlikely if wearing an amulet,
    but you never know about future versions, or I might be missing an
    odd exception), the amulet is destroyed, the hero slips on a bananna
    peel and breaks his or her neck, and an amusing gravestone is
    generated.
8) All soldiers are generated with wands of striking and 1-2 random
    eggs.
9) Keystone Kops are generated with double hit dice and 1-2 random
    eggs.

Hee hee! Of course, this'd be ridiculous to try to implement, but
it -would- be a counterbalance to the Amulet of Life Saving, and
be potentially useful to chaotics if they're careful.

